Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Fix double-slash dataset URLs for FashionMNIST/CIFAR10 +
 add datasets-sources tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

datasets-sources.js built FashionMNIST and CIFAR10 paths as cdnDir+"/fashion_mnist/..."
and cdnDir+"/cifar10/...". Because the default cdnDir ("https://datasets.nnvp.io/datasets/")
ends with a slash, those produced double-slash URLs ("datasets//fashion_mnist/..."), unlike
MNIST which correctly used cdnDir+"mnist/...". Many CDNs/object stores treat "//" as a distinct
missing path and 404 — a real hazard given the planned Netlify->OVH hosting migration. Removed the
leading slashes so all datasets match MNIST's correct relative form.

Added tests/unit/datasets-sources.test.js (3 tests): verifies the expected datasets exist with a
config + description, that every image/label URL is well-formed with no double slash after the
scheme (fails before this fix), and that each dataset lives under its own directory.

Verified: 28 unit tests pass (25 + 3 new), lint 0/0, build ok.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
